Gave the password form a width and its fields a visible underline. The form is a flex item of the login stack, and a flex item with an auto margin on the cross axis is sized to its content instead of stretched to the line — so the auto margins that centre it also cost it the width they were centring, and it collapsed to whatever the two fields happened to need. It now declares `width: 80%` outright.

The fields had no border at all. `@plone/components` draws a `TextField`'s border with `var(--border-color)`, defined in that package's `theme.css`, which this add-on never loads: it imports the widget's own stylesheet and nothing else. An undefined custom property makes the `border` shorthand invalid at computed-value time, so the declaration was dropped and the underline this add-on set a width for had no style to draw. The fields now declare the whole border themselves, against a new `--identity-field-border` token that the client-registration and secret-reveal inputs share. @ericof
